  "final_message": "The audit log key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\nHow it gets there:\n- `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` (`service.py:6`).\n- `write_audit` builds the key with `_format_key(kind, ident)` (`audit.py:11`). That function returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n- `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` (`config.py:3`), so the key is `AUD` + `ORDER` + `7781`, joined with hyphens.\n\nThe `key =[REDACTED:SECRET]'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`. `decoy_metrics.py` uses the `MET` prefix but writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log, and `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
